# Curio environment example — copy to your environment (local shell or GitHub
# Actions secrets) as needed.
#
# The app itself NEVER needs these to build or run: every network feature
# works keyless with a lower quota. Add GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY only if you want
# more reliable Google Books lookups (book covers + ratings) — the free tier
# is plenty for the catalog size.

# Optional: Google Books API key (free, keyless fallback stays active when unset)
# https://developers.google.com/books/docs/v1/using#APIKey
GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=

# Optional: LibraryThing developer key (free) — enables the LibraryThing
# cover provider (ISBN-based, covers.librarything.com). Unset hides that
# provider row; every other provider stays keyless.
# https://www.librarything.com/services/keys.php
LIBRARY_THING_API_KEY=

# Optional: Spotify developer credentials (free) — enables REAL Spotify
# album/track/artist deep links (client-credentials flow, no user auth).
# Create an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard and paste its
# Client ID + Client Secret. Unset = Spotify keeps using search links.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Release signing (only used by the Android CI pipeline; a keystore is NOT
# required to build locally — Gradle falls back to the debug signing config).
# KEYSTORE_BASE64=
# KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
# KEY_ALIAS=
# KEY_PASSWORD=